WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.816
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.690
PRESENTER: In the
1880s, Italians

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.775
developed special
machines to make espresso.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.870
As the name implies,
this coffee drink

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.940
can be produced in seconds.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.720
Soon the appeal of this quick
brew expanded beyond Italy.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.780
And today espresso is
enjoyed all over the world.

00:00:25.166 --> 00:00:27.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:31.290
Making good espresso is as
much a science as it is an art.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.130
Professional machines
balanced temperature and steam

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:38.730
pressure to produce espresso
with kick and crema.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.810
Professional espresso
machines are made

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.030
of high carbon steel sheets.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.670
Computer program tools
carve different shapes

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.930
out of the steel.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.550
These parts will
be the framework

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.720
for the espresso machine.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:59.150
The tools also cut holes for
screws, bolts, and components,

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.170
like the steam tab.

00:01:04.069 --> 00:01:07.100
An employee places a
freshly cut control panel

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.930
into a hydraulic press machine.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:13.690
The press bends the panel
to the correct shape

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.370
and creates tabs for assembly.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.030
This is the panel before
and after bending.

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.240
After bending the other panels,
they assemble the framework.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.790
The worker attaches a receptacle
to capture excess water.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.840
He installs meters to
control the flow of water.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.110
They release different amounts
for long or short espressos.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.510
He turns the base right
side up and screws

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.980
the side framework to it.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.115
He attaches the front
panel to the sides.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.715
The espresso machine's
framework is now in place.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.350
Next, they make the group heads.

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.199
These parts will shoot
hot pressurized water

00:02:09.199 --> 00:02:10.699
through the packed
ground coffee.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:16.130
The worker installs valves that
will regulate the water flow.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.710
The valves also release
built up pressure

00:02:18.710 --> 00:02:21.680
so that the filter holders
can be removed after brewing.

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.484
The group heads fit into slots
in the front of the framework.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.490
He secures them with
nuts at the back.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:40.390
He places a large
copper and brass

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:43.810
boiler in the espresso
machine chassis

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.150
and connects the water lines.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.680
The tank will generate steam
to froth milk for cappuccinos.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.830
It will also supply
hot water for tea.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:56.320
Heat exchangers run through
the boiler to supply

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:57.610
the hot water for brewing.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.210
He connects copper pipes
to the heat exchanger

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.950
outlets on the boiler.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:06.040
Then he links them
to the group heads.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.560
The pipes have been
pre-bend in order to easily

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:09.970
fit into the group heads.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.510
He tightens the fitting
for the hot water tap.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.180
Next, he installs the pump
that pressurizes the water.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.786
He screws it to one
side of the framework.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:31.120
A worker then wires
the electronics

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.250
to the front of the machine.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:42.260
The employee fits the control
panel to the front framework.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:50.580
He slips rubber molding
around the protruding seam.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.545
Then he screws knobs
onto the levers.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.765
He tucks heating coil into
the upper part of a machine.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.720
The top of the machine
works as a cup warmer.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:08.320
The espresso stays hot longer
when served in heated cups.

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:13.330
A worker then encases the
steel espresso machine and

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.815
polycarbonate molded panels.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.700
The plastic parts are slightly
rounded to make the espresso

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:21.930
machine look less boxy.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.700
He seats a steel drip tray
under the group heads.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.740
And he places the cup tray
over the heating element.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:42.000
The espresso machine is ready
for the filter basket holders.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.910
They're equipped with winglets
that hook into the group heads.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:51.320
The worker tests
the espresso machine

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:53.150
to confirm that
there are no leaks

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:54.530
in the hydraulic circuitry.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.570
The machine appears to
be in good working order.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.610
Now it's time for
a coffee break.

